(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test10_2A"] = [{"id":"1695391a","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The following text is from Alice Kaplan’s 1993 memoir French Lessons. When I started to talk on my own, I couldn’t be stopped. When I was in first grade, my sister’s friends could hardly stand to ride to school with me in the car. I was loud and unrelenting. ©1993 by The University of Chicago As used in the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Alice Kaplan’s 1993 memoir French Lessons.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"When I started to talk on my own, I couldn’t be stopped. When I was in first grade, my sister’s friends could hardly stand to ride to","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"school with me in the car. I was loud and unrelenting.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©1993 by The University of Chicago","indent":4}],"question":"As used in the text, what does the author most nearly mean by “I couldn’t be stopped”?","choices":["She had a hard time sitting still.","She often changed her mind.","She was well liked as a child.","She seemed to talk all the time."],"underline":"I couldn’t be stopped.","underline_segments":["I couldn’t be stopped."]},{"id":"79fe7550","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Researcher Haesung Jung led a 2020 study showing that individual acts of kindness can ______ prosocial behavior across a larger group. Jung and her team found that bystanders who witness a helpful act become more likely to offer help to someone else, and in doing so, can inspire still others to act.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Researcher Haesung Jung led a 2020 study showing that individual acts of kindness can ______ prosocial behavior across a larger group. Jung","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and her team found that bystanders who witness a helpful act become more likely to offer help to someone else, and in doing so, can inspire still","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"others to act.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["require","remember","foster","discourage"]},{"id":"a60b0004","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Scholarly discussions of gender in Shakespeare’s comedies often celebrate the rebellion of the playwright’s characters against the rigid expectations ______ by Elizabethan society. Most of the comedies end in marriage, with characters returning to their socially dictated gender roles after previously defying them, but there are some notable exceptions.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Scholarly discussions of gender in Shakespeare’s comedies often celebrate the rebellion of the playwright’s characters against the rigid","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"expectations ______ by Elizabethan society. Most of the comedies end in marriage, with characters returning to their socially dictated gender","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"roles after previously defying them, but there are some notable exceptions.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["interjected","committed","illustrated","prescribed"]},{"id":"3118ca93","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The fashion resale market, in which consumers purchase secondhand clothing from stores and online sellers, generated nearly $30 billion globally in 2019. Expecting to see continued growth, some analysts ______ that revenues will more than double by 2028.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The fashion resale market, in which consumers purchase secondhand clothing from stores and online sellers, generated nearly $30 billion","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"globally in 2019. Expecting to see continued growth, some analysts ______ that revenues will more than double by 2028.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["produced","denied","worried","predicted"]},{"id":"4c4db685","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"On painter William H. Johnson’s return to the United States in 1938 after a decade in Europe, his style underwent an abrupt transformation. Turning away from landscapes painted in an expressionist style — a style that often involves using fluid, distorted shapes and thick, textured brushstrokes to express the artist’s subjective experience of reality — Johnson began painting portraits of Black Americans in a bold new way. Evocative of African sculpture and American and Scandinavian folk art, these portraits feature flat, deliberately oversimplified figures in a vibrant but limited color palette.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"On painter William H. Johnson’s return to the United States in 1938 after a decade in Europe, his style underwent an abrupt transformation.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Turning away from landscapes painted in an expressionist style—a style that often involves using fluid, distorted shapes and thick, textured","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"brushstrokes to express the artist’s subjective experience of reality—Johnson began painting portraits of Black Americans in a bold new way.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Evocative of African sculpture and American and Scandinavian folk art, these portraits feature flat, deliberately oversimplified figures in a vibrant","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"but limited color palette.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It elaborates on the previous sentence’s statement about a transitional moment in Johnson’s artistic career.","It provides information about Johnson’s travels in support of a claim about his artistic influences, which is advanced in the following sentence.","It recounts a moment in Johnson’s personal life that enabled the success of his subsequent career, which is summarized in the following sentence.","It presents evidence that calls into question the previous sentence’s characterization of Johnson’s artistic development."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Turning away from landscapes painted in an expressionist style—a style that often involves using fluid, distorted shapes and thick, textured","brushstrokes to express the artist’s subjective experience of reality—Johnson began painting portraits of Black Americans in a bold new way."]},{"id":"eae66bf9","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 In 2021, a team led by Amir Siraj hypothesized that the Chicxulub impactor — the object that struck the Yucat án Peninsula sixty-six million years ago, precipitating the mass extinction of the dinosaurs — was likely a member of the class of long-period comets. As evidence, Siraj cited the carbonaceous chondritic composition of samples from the Chicxulub impact crater as well as of samples obtained from long-period comet Wild 2 in 2006. Text 2 Although long-period comets contain carbonaceous chondrites, asteroids are similarly rich in these materials. Furthermore, some asteroids are rich in iridium, as Natalia Artemieva points out, whereas long-period comets are not. Given the prevalence of iridium at the crater and, more broadly, in geological layers deposited worldwide following the impact, Artemieva argues that an asteroid is a more plausible candidate for the Chicxulub impactor.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"In 2021, a team led by Amir Siraj hypothesized that the Chicxulub impactor—the object that struck the Yucatán Peninsula sixty-six million years","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ago, precipitating the mass extinction of the dinosaurs—was likely a member of the class of long-period comets. As evidence, Siraj cited the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"carbonaceous chondritic composition of samples from the Chicxulub impact crater as well as of samples obtained from long-period comet Wild","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"2 in 2006.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Although long-period comets contain carbonaceous chondrites, asteroids are similarly rich in these materials. Furthermore, some asteroids are","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rich in iridium, as Natalia Artemieva points out, whereas long-period comets are not. Given the prevalence of iridium at the crater and, more","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"broadly, in geological layers deposited worldwide following the impact, Artemieva argues that an asteroid is a more plausible candidate for the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Chicxulub impactor.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, how would Artemieva likely respond to Siraj’s hypothesis, as presented in Text 1?","choices":["By insisting that it overestimates how representative Wild 2 is of long-period comets as a class","By arguing that it does not account for the amount of iridium found in geological layers dating to the Chicxulub impact","By praising it for connecting the composition of Chicxulub crater samples to the composition of certain asteroids","By concurring that carbonaceous chondrites are prevalent in soil samples from sites distant from the Chicxulub crater"]},{"id":"2e8ab360","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Eighteenth-century historian Edward Gibbon thought the only character defect of the Roman emperor Marcus Aurelius was his mild temperament —though the emperor was widely considered virtuous, his overly permissive nature led him to ______ the vices of those who surrounded him.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Eighteenth-century historian Edward Gibbon thought the only character defect of the Roman emperor Marcus Aurelius was his mild temperament","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"—though the emperor was widely considered virtuous, his overly permissive nature led him to ______ the vices of those who surrounded him.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["indulge","despise","moderate","criticize"]},{"id":"e1e89221","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The following text is from Frances Hodgson Burnett’s 1911 novel The Secret Garden. Mary, a young girl, is outside trying her new jump rope. The sun was shining and a little wind was blowing — not a rough wind, but one which came in delightful little gusts and brought a fresh scent of newly turned earth with it. She skipped round the fountain garden, and up one walk and down another. As used in the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Frances Hodgson Burnett’s 1911 novel The Secret Garden. Mary, a young girl, is outside trying her new jump rope.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The sun was shining and a little wind was blowing—not a rough wind, but one which came in delightful little gusts and brought a","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"fresh scent of newly turned earth with it. She skipped round the fountain garden, and up one walk and down another.","indent":2}],"question":"As used in the text, what does the word “rough” most nearly mean?","choices":["Harsh","Scratchy","Basic","Vague"],"underline":"rough","underline_segments":["rough"]},{"id":"0113152f","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"American fashion designer Patrick Kelly was known for his love of colorful buttons. Many of his signature dresses feature bold assortments of buttons throughout the garment. In a paper, a fashion design student claims that Kelly’s use of buttons as decoration was inspired by his childhood observations of the styles and actions of the women in his family. Which quotation from a work by a historian would be the most effective evidence for","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"American fashion designer Patrick Kelly was known for his love of colorful buttons. Many of his signature dresses feature bold assortments of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"buttons throughout the garment. In a paper, a fashion design student claims that Kelly’s use of buttons as decoration was inspired by his","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"childhood observations of the styles and actions of the women in his family.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation would be the most effective evidence for the student to include in support of this claim?","choices":["“Although some of the assortments of buttons appear to be mismatched pieces scattered randomly throughout Kelly’s dresses, his most famous designs feature carefully crafted patterns of matching buttons.”","“Many of Kelly’s contemporaries were inspired by his designs to incorporate buttons, as well as zippers and snaps, as decorative items in their work.”","“Kelly’s grandmother, who would repair clothing when he was a child, frequently added mismatched buttons to the clothes to draw attention away from any flaws in the garments.”","“Kelly was destined to be a designer from a young age: he learned how to sew clothing from his aunt Bertha, and his love of drawing was developed by his mother.”"]},{"id":"714e4c10","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Ruth Asawa was an accomplished artist who worked in many art forms, including her unique tied-wire sculptures, but she was dedicated to more than the creation of art. Asawa also wanted to bring art to children in her hometown of San Francisco, California. To that end, in 1968 she cofounded the Alvarado School Arts Workshop, which brought works of art and artists into public schools, and in 1982 she helped found a San Francisco public arts high school, which was later named after her.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Ruth Asawa was an accomplished artist who worked in many art forms, including her unique tied-wire sculptures, but she was dedicated to more","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"than the creation of art. Asawa also wanted to bring art to children in her hometown of San Francisco, California. To that end, in 1968 she","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"cofounded the Alvarado School Arts Workshop, which brought works of art and artists into public schools, and in 1982 she helped found a San","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Francisco public arts high school, which was later named after her.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["Asawa inspired many other artists to share their work with students in public schools.","Asawa’s unique sculptures were appreciated more by local art communities than they were nationwide.","Asawa’s interest in art education prompted her to create art programs for students in San Francisco.","Asawa left a promising career as a sculptor to work as an art teacher in San Francisco schools."]},{"id":"b38935ab","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Historians point to the rule of the Piast dynasty as crucial to the formation of the Polish state. However, some differentiate between members of the dynasty like Mieszko II Lambert, who ruled as king from 1025 to 1031 CE, and less well-documented figures like Siemomysł, who is said to have ruled in the 10th century but whose historical actuality is disputed. Siemomysł appears in the Gesta principum Polonorum, a chronicle of medieval Polish history written between 1112 and 1118. However, the chronicle’s documentation of Siemomysł relies on oral tradition, unlike its records of later rulers. According to the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Historians point to the rule of the Piast dynasty as crucial to the formation of the Polish state. However, some differentiate between members of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the dynasty like Mieszko II Lambert, who ruled as king from 1025 to 1031 CE, and less well-documented figures like Siemomysł, who is said to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"have ruled in the 10th century but whose historical actuality is disputed. Siemomysł appears in the Gesta principum Polonorum, a chronicle of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"medieval Polish history written between 1112 and 1118. However, the chronicle’s documentation of Siemomysł relies on oral tradition, unlike its","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"records of later rulers.","indent":0}],"question":"According to the text, what is a difference between how historians view Siemomysł and how they view Mieszko II Lambert?","choices":["Historians agree that Mieszko II Lambert existed, but disagree about whether Siemomysł existed.","Historians believe that the Gesta principum Polonorum provides more evidence for Siemomysł s existence than it does for Mieszko II Lambert’s existence.","Historians agree that Siemomysł ruled Poland much later than Mieszko II Lambert.","Historians find the orally transmitted stories affirming the existence of Mieszko II Lambert to be more convincing than similar stories about Siemomysł."]},{"id":"e441da80","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Investigative Articles Published in the Albuquerque Journal from 2010 to 2019 1,750 1,500 Number of articles 1,250 1,000 750 500 250 0 10 011 012 013 014 015 016 017 018 019 20 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 Total Investigative journalists research and report about fraud, corruption, public hazards, and more. The graph shows the number of investigative articles published in the Albuquerque Journal newspaper from 2010 to 2019. According to an analyst, although the number of investigative articles published in this newspaper has varied significantly over the period shown, the number overall has fallen since 2010.","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Investigative Articles Published in the Albuquerque Journal, 2010–2019 — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Investigative journalists research and report about fraud, corruption, public hazards, and more. The graph shows the number of investigative articles published in the Albuquerque Journal newspaper from 2010 to 2019. According to an analyst, although the number of investigative articles published in this newspaper has varied significantly over the period shown, the number overall has fallen since 2010."}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to justify the underlined claim?","choices":["The newspaper published approximately 1,000 investigative articles in 2010 and approximately 500 in 2019.","The smallest annual number of investigative articles published in the newspaper during the period shown is approximately 1,600 in 2013.","The greatest annual number of investigative articles published in the newspaper during the period shown is approximately 1,000 in 2017.","The newspaper published approximately 1,000 investigative articles in 2010 and approximately 1,600 in 2013."],"underline":"the number overall has fallen since 2010.","underline_segments":["the number overall has fallen since 2010."]},{"id":"0fd96039","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"It has long been thought that the original author of the US Pledge of Allegiance was Francis Bellamy, who said that he wrote the pledge one evening in August of 1892. But a historian recently discovered a newspaper article that was published several months before August 1892. The article describes students reciting the same pledge that Bellamy claims he first wrote in August. This means that Bellamy may not have created the pledge after all.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"It has long been thought that the original author of the US Pledge of Allegiance was Francis Bellamy, who said that he wrote the pledge one","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"evening in August of 1892. But a historian recently discovered a newspaper article that was published several months before August 1892. The","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"article describes students reciting the same pledge that Bellamy claims he first wrote in August. This means that Bellamy may not have created","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the pledge after all.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the text, what piece of knowledge about the Pledge of Allegiance has recently become uncertain?","choices":["How many changes were made to the pledge in the 1900s","The identity of the person who first wrote the pledge","The name of the newspaper that first published the pledge","Which part of the pledge students liked best in 1892"]},{"id":"b7d51f84","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"In West Africa, jalis have traditionally been keepers of information about family histories and records of important events. They have often served as teachers and advisers, too. New technologies may have changed some aspects of the role today, but jalis continue to be valued for knowing and protecting their peoples’ stories.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In West Africa, jalis have traditionally been keepers of information about family histories and records of important events. They have often served","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"as teachers and advisers, too. New technologies may have changed some aspects of the role today, but jalis continue to be valued for knowing","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and protecting their peoples’ stories.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["Even though there have been some changes in their role, jalis continue to preserve their communities’ histories.","Although jalis have many roles, many of them like teaching best.","Jalis have been entertaining the people within their communities for centuries.","Technology can now do some of the things jalis used to be responsible for."]},{"id":"8a584241","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Seed Germination with and without H₂S Treatment 100 90 Seeds germinated (%) 80 70 60 50 40 30 20 10 0 24 48 72 168 Time (hours) 500 micromoles per liter 10 micromoles per liter untreated In high concentrations, hydrogen sulfide (H₂S) is typically toxic to many plants. Frederick D. Dooley and colleagues wanted to understand what effects low doses of H₂S might have on plant growth. They treated bean, corn, wheat, and pea seeds with various concentrations (measured in micromoles per liter) of H₂S and tracked the germination of those seeds along with the germination of untreated seeds. Treatment with particular concentrations of H₂S was associated with accelerated germination: for example, ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Seed Germination with and without H₂S Treatment — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"In high concentrations, hydrogen sulfide (H₂S) is typically toxic to many plants. Frederick D. Dooley and colleagues wanted to understand what effects low doses of H₂S might have on plant growth. They treated bean, corn, wheat, and pea seeds with various concentrations (measured in micromoles per liter) of H₂S and tracked the germination of those seeds along with the germination of untreated seeds. Treatment with particular concentrations of H₂S was associated with accelerated germination: for example, ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the statement?","choices":["at 24 hours, less than 10% of seeds treated with H₂S at a concentration of 10 micromoles per liter had germinated, whereas more than 90% of those seeds had germinated at 168 hours.","at 48 hours, more than 70% of seeds treated with H₂S at a concentration of 10 micromoles per liter had germinated, whereas only approximately 50% of untreated seeds had germinated.","at 168 hours, more than 90% of seeds treated with H₂S at concentrations of 10 or 500 micromoles per liter had germinated, whereas less than 70% of untreated seeds had germinated.",""],"unusable":"missing graph"},{"id":"267a13e2","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In 2010, archaeologist Noel Hidalgo Tan was visiting the twelfth-century temple of Angkor Wat in Cambodia when he noticed markings of red paint on the temple ______ the help of digital imaging techniques, he discovered the markings to be part of an elaborate mural containing over 200 paintings.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2010, archaeologist Noel Hidalgo Tan was visiting the twelfth-century temple of Angkor Wat in Cambodia when he noticed markings of red","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"paint on the temple ______ the help of digital imaging techniques, he discovered the markings to be part of an elaborate mural containing over","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"200 paintings.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["walls, with","walls with","walls so with","walls. With"]},{"id":"1ee4485c","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Journalists have dubbed Gil Scott-Heron the “godfather of rap,” a title that has appeared in hundreds of articles about him since the 1990s. Scott- Heron himself resisted the godfather ______ feeling that it didn’t encapsulate his devotion to the broader African American blues music tradition as well as “bluesologist,” the moniker he preferred.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Journalists have dubbed Gil Scott-Heron the “godfather of rap,” a title that has appeared in hundreds of articles about him since the 1990s. Scott-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Heron himself resisted the godfather ______ feeling that it didn’t encapsulate his devotion to the broader African American blues music tradition","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"as well as “bluesologist,” the moniker he preferred.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["nickname, however","nickname, however;","nickname, however,","nickname; however,"]},{"id":"36944347","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Official measurements of the Mississippi River’s length vary: according to the US Geologic Survey, the river is 2,300 miles long, whereas the Environmental Protection Agency records its length as 2,320 miles. This disparity can be explained in part by the fact that rivers such as the Mississippi expand and contract as ______ sediment.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Official measurements of the Mississippi River’s length vary: according to the US Geologic Survey, the river is 2,300 miles long, whereas the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Environmental Protection Agency records its length as 2,320 miles. This disparity can be explained in part by the fact that rivers such as the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Mississippi expand and contract as ______ sediment.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["they accumulate","one accumulates","it accumulates","we accumulate"]},{"id":"9eb43963","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Water in the North Atlantic Ocean is pushed eastward by powerful winds, but the rotation of Earth and interference from nearby landmasses together cause ______ to swirl into a massive, churning whirlpool — also called the North Atlantic Gyre — that spins clockwise.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Water in the North Atlantic Ocean is pushed eastward by powerful winds, but the rotation of Earth and interference from nearby landmasses","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"together cause ______ to swirl into a massive, churning whirlpool—also called the North Atlantic Gyre—that spins clockwise.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["these","those","them","it"]},{"id":"c04e9136","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"The 2022 Nobel Prize in Chemistry was awarded to three pioneers in the field of click chemistry: two-time Nobel laureate Barry Sharpless, who coined the term “click chemistry” in 1998; Carolyn Bertozzi, founder of the Bertozzi Group at ______ and Morten Meldal, a professor at the University of Copenhagen in Denmark.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The 2022 Nobel Prize in Chemistry was awarded to three pioneers in the field of click chemistry: two-time Nobel laureate Barry Sharpless, who","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"coined the term “click chemistry” in 1998; Carolyn Bertozzi, founder of the Bertozzi Group at ______ and Morten Meldal, a professor at the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"University of Copenhagen in Denmark.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Stanford","Stanford,","Stanford:","Stanford;"]},{"id":"9579581e","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"As cheesemaking practices spread throughout Europe and Asia during and after the Neolithic, divergent strategies for preserving milk ______ whereas rennet-coagulated cheesemaking became key to milk preservation in Europe and Southwest Asia, acid-heat coagulation methods became common among nomadic herding populations of the northeastern Eurasian steppe.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["emerged","emerged and","emerged:","emerged,"]},{"id":"34a5ba1c","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"By 1936, Spanish Romani dancer Carmen Amaya was known all over Spain for her powerful style of flamenco dancing. However, in July of that year, the outbreak of the Spanish Civil War made it difficult for her to perform in her home country. ______ Amaya left Spain to perform abroad, dancing for audiences across North and South America.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"By 1936, Spanish Romani dancer Carmen Amaya was known all over Spain for her powerful style of flamenco dancing. However, in July of that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"year, the outbreak of the Spanish Civil War made it difficult for her to perform in her home country. ______ Amaya left Spain to perform abroad,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"dancing for audiences across North and South America.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In comparison,","As a result,","First of all,","For example,"]},{"id":"146233fc","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Lighthouses send out crucial light signals to help ships and other watercraft navigate at night. Before automation, lighthouses were run by lighthouse keepers. Maria Younghans was the lighthouse keeper at Biloxi Light in Mississippi. She held this position from 1867 to 1918. Flora McNeil was the lighthouse keeper at Bridgeport Breakwater Light in Connecticut. She held this position from 1904 to 1920. The student wants to emphasize the order in which the two lighthouse keepers began their careers.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Lighthouses send out crucial light signals to help ships and other watercraft navigate at night.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Before automation, lighthouses were run by lighthouse keepers.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Maria Younghans was the lighthouse keeper at Biloxi Light in Mississippi.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She held this position from 1867 to 1918.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Flora McNeil was the lighthouse keeper at Bridgeport Breakwater Light in Connecticut.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She held this position from 1904 to 1920.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["From 1867 to 1918, the nighttime waters of Mississippi were more navigable thanks to lighthouse keepers Flora McNeil and Maria Younghans.","Before automation, lighthouse keepers like Maria Younghans and Flora McNeil were crucial to ensuring safe navigation for watercraft.","Flora McNeil began her career as a lighthouse keeper years after Maria Younghans did.","Maria Younghans’s career as a lighthouse keeper ended in 1918, whereas Flora McNeil’s ended in 1920."]},{"id":"1e31470f","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"To perform a quad axel, a figure skater must leap into the air and complete four and a half rotations before landing, an extreme feat. ______ in 2022, when 17-year-old Ilia Malinin landed the first quad axel — considered the most difficult quad jump — in a high-level competition, the audience was left awestruck.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"To perform a quad axel, a figure skater must leap into the air and complete four and a half rotations before landing, an extreme feat. ______ in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"2022, when 17-year-old Ilia Malinin landed the first quad axel—considered the most difficult quad jump—in a high-level competition, the audience","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"was left awestruck.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Moreover,","Fittingly,","Next,","However,"]},{"id":"e3484c07","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Bioluminescence is the emission of light by living organisms. This light is produced by chemical reactions in organisms’ cells. Jellyfish emit flashes of blue light. This behavior serves to startle predators. Black dragonfish emit a steady red light. This behavior helps them locate prey in deep waters. The student wants to emphasize a difference between the behavior of jellyfish and that of black dragonfish.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Bioluminescence is the emission of light by living organisms.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"This light is produced by chemical reactions in organisms’ cells.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Jellyfish emit flashes of blue light.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"This behavior serves to startle predators.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Black dragonfish emit a steady red light.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"This behavior helps them locate prey in deep waters.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both jellyfish and black dragonfish are organisms that emit light, which is produced by chemical reactions in these organisms’ cells.","Black dragonfish emit a steady red light, which helps them locate prey in deep waters.","Bioluminescence, the emission of light by living organisms, results from chemical reactions in organisms’ cells.","Jellyfish emit light to startle predators, whereas black dragonfish do so to locate prey."]},{"id":"1bb4aec8","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Meteorites found on Earth are divided into two categories. A meteorite that was observed falling to Earth before being recovered is known as a meteorite fall. All other meteorites found on Earth are known as meteorite finds. There have been about 1,200 recorded meteorite falls. There have been over 60,000 recorded meteorite finds. The student wants to contrast the number of meteorite falls with the number of meteorite finds.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Meteorites found on Earth are divided into two categories.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"A meteorite that was observed falling to Earth before being recovered is known as a meteorite fall.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"All other meteorites found on Earth are known as meteorite finds.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"There have been about 1,200 recorded meteorite falls.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"There have been over 60,000 recorded meteorite finds.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["A meteorite that was observed falling to Earth before being recovered is known as a meteorite fall; all others are known as meteorite finds.","Meteorites found on Earth are divided into two categories: meteorite falls and meteorite finds.","There have been about 1,200 recorded meteorite falls, or meteorites observed falling to Earth.","While there have been only about 1,200 recorded meteorite falls, there have been over 60,000 meteorite finds."]},{"id":"2b08f514","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"The prime meridian, the global indicator of zero degrees longitude established in 1884, was originally determined using astronomically derived coordinates. ______ as decades passed, new calculations would reveal increasingly precise coordinates, yet the prime meridian remained unchanged; it wasn’t until the 1980s that, spurred by improved geodetic data, the prime meridian was officially moved — roughly one hundred meters east.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The prime meridian, the global indicator of zero degrees longitude established in 1884, was originally determined using astronomically derived","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"coordinates. ______ as decades passed, new calculations would reveal increasingly precise coordinates, yet the prime meridian remained","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"unchanged; it wasn’t until the 1980s that, spurred by improved geodetic data, the prime meridian was officially moved—roughly one hundred","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"meters east.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Specifically,","To that end,","Again and again,","Granted,"]}];
